extraction_notes: "WB17 Warlords of Russia printed 61-64 (cache p062-p065, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer. The stat block starts on printed 63 and ends with Money and Cybernetics on printed 64. || HEADING: Ectohunter O.C.C., also known as Ghost Hunters and spiritualists; listed under Russian Adventurer O.C.C.s on printed 57, so occ_group is optional and men_of_arms is false; the entry states no S.D.C. base. || XP: the Ectohunter, Travelling Story Teller and Warlord Cyber-Doc ladder as given in the brief, read off a render of the Experience Tables on printed 6. || SPECIAL ABILITIES: the eleven numbered Special Ectohunter O.C.C. Abilities (printed 62-63) are stored as special_abilities, except 6 (P.P.E.), which is ppe_base, and 10 (O.C.C. Bonuses), which is split: +1 pull punch is in bonuses, +1 to save vs illusions is saves.other because the book says illusions and not illusionary magic, and +2 initiative against ghostly beings only is conditional and stored as an ability. || HORROR FACTOR: +1 at levels 1-10, 12 and 14 stored as horror_factor 1 plus eleven at_level entries; the book qualifies it as applying to supernatural monsters and horrors, which is stated in the ability and is a reading. || POSSESSION: +10 flat plus +1 at levels 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12 and 14, as printed. || P.P.E.: 4D6 plus the P.E. attribute number, plus 1D4 per level. The class casts no spells of its own (it reads scrolls and uses magic items), so there is no magic block. || PSIONICS: not a requirement; about one third have minor or major psionics; no block and no roll is printed. || VULNERABILITY: the M.E. loss and insanity rolls are in side_effects and an ability; nothing applies them. ''Every other level'' prints no starting level. || SKILLS: Speaks Euro and two other languages of choice (+20%) is read as Euro at +20% and two Language: Other picks at +20%. Surveillance Systems maps to Surveillance, Read Sensory Equipment to Sensory Equipment. Lore: one of choice is one pick across the Lore: rows of Technical and Cowboy. Pilot: one of choice (+5%) offers all of Pilot; the O.C.C. line prints no exclusion. W.P. Energy Weapon of choice is a W.P. category pick with the restriction in the note. || PILOT EXCEPT: ''except robots, power armor, military vehicles, ships and aircraft'' read literally as all ships and all aircraft, mapped to the Robot rows, the Military: rows, Boat: Ships, Airplane, Helicopter, Jet Aircraft, both Fighter Combat rows, the three Space craft rows and Wingrider Flying Wing. Air Assault Armor, Combat Pod, Flight System Combat, Jet Packs and Jump Bike Combat are left available and need a human reading. || TECHNICAL: +10% stored; +15% to language or computer skills is in the note only. || MONEY: 1D6x1000 credits stored (the text layer prints !D6xlOOO); the 1D6x100 in tradeable goods is in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: one M.D. weapon of choice; a box of 100 large resealable plastic bags, clothing, a bedroll, belt, boots, a note pad and personal items have no catalog row. Light suit of M.D.C. body armor maps to light-mdc-body-armor, the pair of silver knives to two knife-silver-plated, the mallet to hammer-and-mallet. || NOT STORED: the fee structure (as little as 100 credits to tens of thousands, a nonrefundable 10% retainer plus expenses), the nationality percentages, and Secret Resources are prose in GM Notes."
---

## Lore

The Ectohunter is a professional ghost hunter: part bounty hunter, part
exterminator, working against spirits, entities and other spectral things
across Russia, Mongolia, China and the rest of Eurasia. Most took up the
trade after a brush with the supernatural that left a mark. Some are grim,
some scholarly, some reckless or jumpy, and a few are as cold as what they
hunt.

Long exposure to the spirit world has changed them. They sense and see
ghostly beings, speak with them mind to mind, and can charge a fist or an
old-fashioned weapon with enough magic energy to hurt something that has no
body. They shrug off fear and possession that would break anyone else. They
can read scrolls and use magic items, but they are not mages.

They work for pay, and they are not shy about it: a retainer up front, room
and board while on the job, and the balance on success. That, and the fact
that a banished ghost leaves no body as proof, means many people think of
them as arrogant and grasping. The work also wears on the mind over time.

## GM Notes

Ghost Killing costs 2 P.P.E. per use, lasts about four melee rounds per level
while the character concentrates, and takes a full melee round to bring up
below 5th level. It affects only ethereal beings and spirit-like essences; it
does nothing against solid M.D.C. demons and monsters, which is why most
Ectohunters will identify such a threat for a small fee but refuse to fight
it, and the half who will fight charge outrageous fees.

The +2 initiative applies only against ghostly beings. The Horror Factor
bonus is printed for supernatural monsters and horrors.

Vulnerability, rolled by hand: every other level, 01-50% to permanently lose
one M.E. point; every third level starting at level three, 01-66% to gain a
random insanity (Random Insanity Table, Rifts RPG page 19).

Fees vary by hunter and danger: as little as 100 credits and a couple of
nights'' hospitality for a minor entity, up to tens of thousands of credits or
more for a great menace. The usual terms are a nonrefundable 10% retainer
plus room and board, with the balance paid only on success; an employer may
keep the hunter in town for days or weeks, at the community''s expense, to see
that the thing is gone.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: one M.D. weapon of choice, a box of
100 large resealable plastic bags for specimens, clothing, bedroll, belt,
boots, a note pad and personal items. Money is 1D6x1000 credits plus 1D6x100
in tradeable goods. The vehicle is a used hovercycle or other basic
transportation missing 1D4x10 M.D.C. from the main body.

No secret resources. Most people dislike Ectohunters as money-grubbing;
Bogatyrs and other humanitarians especially so, and Huntsmen treat them as a
joke. About 30-40% have psionics, by the ability text; the stat block says
about one third have minor or major psionics. Neither prints a roll.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ectohunter');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ectohunter';

